      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "ev_17",
        on: "start",
        once: true,
        children: [
          {
            tag: "hook",
            name: "command:play_music",
            file: "transience.ogg",
            play_once: "yes",
          },
          {
            tag: "hook",
            name: "command:unstore_unit",
            variable: "stored_Baldras",
          },
          {
            tag: "hook",
            name: "command:capture_village",
            side: 1,
            cells: "28,3",
          },
          {
            tag: "hook",
            name: "command:recall_unit",
            id: "Harper",
            unit: "Harper",
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Baldras",
            text: _("Maddock, I be coming to report—"),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Lord Maddock",
            text: _("I am already aware of your altercation in Dallben, Baldras. Your dissent was not wise."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Baldras",
            text: _("Dissent? Maddock, I’m not trusting no strange riders who show up out of nowhere claimin’ to be from the Queen. Seems like a bunch of pigdirt to me."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Lord Maddock",
            text: _("That was partially my fault, since I was not able to send a messenger to you in time. I shall have to inform you now. Five weeks ago, at the Ford of Abez, King Garard II of Wesnoth was murdered."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Lord Maddock",
            text: _("Officially, one of his captains committed the crime. Unofficially, it is rumored that Queen Asheviere and her son Eldred were involved. Either way, Prince Eldred fell in battle not long after, upon which Asheviere claimed the throne."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Lord Maddock",
            text: _("The Queen is not popular. She is at war with supporters of the old king, and searches far and wide for new conscripts. Part of that has been taking elders from the local villages, forcing them to swear allegiance to her. That was the purpose of that patrol."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Baldras",
            text: _("Annuvin province be ruled by Elensefar! We has no duty to Weldyn."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Lord Maddock",
            text: _("You do now. I do not really need to tell you what will happen should you refuse Her Majesty’s offer."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Baldras",
            text: _("Grow a spine, Maddock. If they come to ya and make you swear fealty to this Asheviere, would ya really give up that easy?"),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Lord Maddock",
            text: _("They will not come. I do not intend to pick a side in Wesnoth’s conflict, and the Queen knows better than to try to force my hand. It is true that she maintains a large garrison south at the great fortress of Halstead, but even should they mobilize all their troops, I doubt they could take Elensefar."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Harper",
            text: _("But we can’t do nothing! The Queen even be sending them beast orcs against us, that’s how evil she is! Surely you can’t stand for this..."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Lord Maddock",
            text: _("Yes, I am aware of Queen Asheviere’s propensity for hiring orcs to supplement her forces. I have begun expanding my army as well, although I think hostilities are unlikely. But the population of Elensefar is small, and we are not in the habit of maintaining a large standing army. It will take time to assemble mercenaries of the right caliber."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Lord Maddock",
            text: _("The treaty between Elensefar and Wesnoth is ancient, and I do not think Her Majesty means to break it. But I cannot afford to make enemies of Weldyn, as you can surely understand. Asheviere looks to be winning her civil war. The wizard and his rebels have suffered several defeats. I have some concessions that I shall have to make..."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Baldras",
            text: _("And what abouts us? Throw us like dogs to those Wesnothians?"),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Lord Maddock",
            text: _("Do not put words in my mouth. I am more than willing to act should the need arise. I am already in covert communication with— ...listen, there is a bigger picture here, Baldras."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Baldras",
            text: _("The bigger picture of you idly sittin’ here waiting till them Wesnothians come to take the city right from your hands."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Lord Maddock",
            text: _("I very much doubt they would be bold enough to attack us outright—"),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Baldras",
            text: _("Head out of your behind, Maddock. Open your eyes! Look south and tell me that again!"),
          },
          {
            tag: "hook",
            name: "command:scroll_to_unit",
            id: "Kestrel",
          },
          {
            tag: "hook",
            name: "command:delay",
            time: 1000,
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Lord Maddock",
            text: _("An invading army? No, something is not right with those soldiers... but I presume we have no time to ponder that. To arms!"),
          },
        ],
      },
